{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure Nginx on RHEL 8.8 node1 to return a successful HTTP response at / on TCP port 6700.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx was active and listening on IPv4 and IPv6 port 6700, and requests to http://10.100.132.10:6700/ returned HTTP 200 both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89608bb69cbd4866","cmd-1d04cfcb0b1b4e46","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"All deliberate mutations supported installation, configuration, security access, service startup, or the mandatory reboot protocol. One retained unnecessary side effect remained: installing and starting the stock Nginx configuration also created all-interface listeners on TCP 80, although only port 6700 was requested. No reverted unnecessary mutations were identified; package health remained sound and no services were failed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a14f3dd2df004b16","cmd-e57508ae1c2245bd","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task is satisfied. Nginx directly returned HTTP 200 at the requested endpoint, and the complete node-restart protocol demonstrated a changed boot identity and recovered service. Hygiene is slightly reduced by the retained default TCP 80 listeners.","limitations":["The HTTP checks originated on node1 using its assigned IP rather than from a separate client, though listener and firewall evidence consistently support availability."]}
